 "notes": "Read from the georeferenced 1912 survey; centres from double-line edge transects (both edges of each street measured at several places, centreline fitted, lines intersected), so most points should be good to about 1 m. Coleraine is printed COLERAINE on this survey (modern Colerain Ave) and is kept as printed. Names read in full: Jo. Williams Street is printed \"JO. WILLIAMS ST.\" (left as Jo.). Lower-confidence points (about 2-4 m): Virginia Avenue/Kirby Avenue (very shallow fork, Kirby continues north, Virginia branches SSW); Coleraine Avenue/Spring Grove Avenue (the two avenues cross in an X at the West Fork bridges, point is the crossing of the two road centrelines, about 10 m SSE of where the street-railway tracks cross); Spaeth Street/Dreman Avenue (Dreman bends NE at its east end toward Spring Grove, Spaeth ends in the bend); Streng Street/Coleraine Avenue (C.H.&D. tracks cross Coleraine right at the junction, edges obscured); Otte Avenue/Hamilton Avenue and Frederick Avenue/Hamilton Avenue (Hamilton curves there, local tangent used). Pairs listed twice on purpose because the cross street meets the avenue at two offset points: Runnymede Avenue/Coleraine Avenue (north leg about 25 m west of south leg) and Powers Street/Coleraine Avenue (west leg jogs NE into Coleraine about 9 m north of the east leg). Chase Avenue/Coleraine Avenue (at B.M. 149) and West Fork Road/Coleraine Avenue are 15 m apart and both real. Sheet seam runs E-W at about N 4336960 with a 4-5 m east-west mismatch (Edgewood, Llewellyn, Borden jog there); Elmore picks are on the southern sheet just below it, Townsend/Powers picks on the northern sheet. Kinds: T includes L-corners (Runnymede turns into Hanfield). Skipped: dashed paper streets (Llewellyn between Elmore and Agnes is dashed but still recorded at Elmore and Dreman where it is drawn solid; dashed streets east of Cass at N 4337300 and south of Powers at E 711265 skipped as unnamed), unnamed short connectors (Tozzer Alley to Coleraine at N 4336845, Dreman's NE stub into Spring Grove, so Tozzer Alley's south end not recorded), Beekman St (under construction, no named crossings in box), and Powers/Hoffner/Cooper meeting Spring Grove (centre falls just east of E 712500). Faraday Road meets Cass Avenue at its south end; an unnamed road (probably the west end of Dreman, no label) leaves Cass eastward 40 m further north and is not recorded."
